1
00:00:48,103 --> 00:00:49,814
Somebody once said

2
00:00:49,980 --> 00:00:52,942
that religion was deemed
by the commoners as true,

3
00:00:53,108 --> 00:00:54,693
by the wise as false,

4
00:00:54,902 --> 00:00:57,154
and by the rulers as useful.

5
00:01:03,202 --> 00:01:04,829
The only thing
I believe

6
00:01:05,037 --> 00:01:07,623
is that my name
is Jonathan Preest.

7
00:01:07,832 --> 00:01:11,877
And tonight,
I'm gonna kill a man.

8
00:02:29,538 --> 00:02:31,123
- Hey.
- Hey.

9
00:02:34,126 --> 00:02:35,878
What's going on? Where's Karen?

10
00:02:36,045 --> 00:02:38,047
A bit of a change of plan.

11
00:02:39,215 --> 00:02:42,259
Actually, quite a radical one.

12
00:02:42,426 --> 00:02:44,094
What?

13
00:02:46,597 --> 00:02:48,224
You're fucking kidding me?

14
00:02:48,349 --> 00:02:50,184
Seriously, I'm not.

15
00:02:50,309 --> 00:02:54,230
Let's just get back to London.
I think I need a drink.

16
00:03:03,239 --> 00:03:05,115
I think you make
too many demands on me.

17
00:03:06,450 --> 00:03:08,202
I feel we don't connect.

18
00:03:09,912 --> 00:03:11,288
That you...

19
00:03:12,164 --> 00:03:13,290
Sorry.

20
00:03:13,457 --> 00:03:16,460
..I hate you

21
00:03:16,627 --> 00:03:18,254
because of the divorce.

22
00:03:20,422 --> 00:03:24,468
Even though I've done everything to
help you support your so-called career...

23
00:03:24,635 --> 00:03:26,095
Margaret.

24
00:03:26,262 --> 00:03:28,097
Now, remember, remember the rules.

25
00:03:28,264 --> 00:03:32,143
Just what you feel Emilia thinks,
not what you think.

26
00:03:32,268 --> 00:03:34,186
I'm sorry.

27
00:03:34,603 --> 00:03:38,482
It's just that...
I really don't feel I'm getting through.

28
00:03:38,649 --> 00:03:40,818
That is the point of this, isn't it?

29
00:03:40,985 --> 00:03:42,820
Building trust takes time.

30
00:03:42,987 --> 00:03:47,158
All structure must start with foundation,

31
00:03:47,283 --> 00:03:49,869
and communication is
the cornerstone of foundation.

32
00:03:50,035 --> 00:03:51,078
Amen.

33
00:03:57,459 --> 00:03:58,627
Emilia.

34
00:04:01,463 --> 00:04:03,257
For fucking real?

35
00:04:03,382 --> 00:04:05,801
As real as you feel
you would express yourself

36
00:04:05,968 --> 00:04:07,970
if you were in your mother's shoes.

37
00:04:08,512 --> 00:04:09,597
Try.

38
00:04:09,805 --> 00:04:10,973
OK.

39
00:04:16,812 --> 00:04:20,441
The next time that you come back
from hospital after another...

40
00:04:20,608 --> 00:04:23,486
drunken suicide attempt, you little slut,

41
00:04:23,652 --> 00:04:25,654
I'll drag you home,

42
00:04:25,863 --> 00:04:29,074
throw your charity shop cast-offs
into a bin liner,

43
00:04:29,241 --> 00:04:32,036
and make you move
to some other stinking city.

44
00:04:32,203 --> 00:04:34,455
Any excuse to keep us away
from your dear father.

45
00:04:34,622 --> 00:04:37,124
- Don't you start...
- We can't even mention Father now!

46
00:04:37,291 --> 00:04:40,586
- That's enough!
- So we don't have to communicate...

47
00:04:40,794 --> 00:04:43,088
- Emilia!
- ..I'll provide my...my psychotic,

48
00:04:43,255 --> 00:04:45,799
alcoholic, waste-of-fucking-life
daughter...

49
00:04:45,966 --> 00:04:48,427
- Enough!
- ..with a ?00-an-hour psychiatrist.

50
00:04:48,594 --> 00:04:52,306
- You see what I have to deal with?
- Make friends, find yourself a man...

51
00:04:52,431 --> 00:04:54,183
Emilia, will you be quiet?

52
00:04:56,143 --> 00:04:58,062
A little too much?

53
00:05:00,314 --> 00:05:02,399
Emilia, please.

54
00:05:02,566 --> 00:05:05,152
I need to speak with your mother.

55
00:05:07,446 --> 00:05:09,448
See you next Tuesday.

56
00:05:29,593 --> 00:05:31,428
Hello?
- Hello. Anne?

57
00:05:31,595 --> 00:05:33,305
- Peter.
- Er, yes.

58
00:05:33,430 --> 00:05:34,682
You're there. Um...

59
00:05:34,890 --> 00:05:37,643
- I thought we agreed not to do this.
- Yes, but please, wait.

60
00:05:37,852 --> 00:05:40,229
But you promised me
you would not try to contact me.

61
00:05:40,396 --> 00:05:41,814
It's David.

62
00:05:41,981 --> 00:05:43,983
They're letting him do a day visit.

63
00:05:44,150 --> 00:05:46,652
- Yes, I heard.
- I'm picking him up on Wednesday.

64
00:05:48,362 --> 00:05:50,281
He can stay overnight as well.

65
00:05:51,615 --> 00:05:56,871
- Look, Peter, Martin will be home soon.
- Oh, Martin will understand. Ha!

66
00:05:57,037 --> 00:05:58,622
Will you come?

67
00:05:58,831 --> 00:06:01,667
- Peter...
- I'm sure he'd like to see his mother.

68
00:06:02,626 --> 00:06:04,295
Well, I'd like to see you, too.

69
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:07,173
- It's been so long.
- I don't know.

70
00:06:08,132 --> 00:06:09,925
Look, I'll think about it.

71
00:06:10,092 --> 00:06:11,886
I've got to go now.

72
00:06:12,052 --> 00:06:13,220
Yes, OK.

73
00:06:13,387 --> 00:06:16,015
Don't read too much into this.

74
00:06:16,974 --> 00:06:19,101
I'll expect your call, then.

75
00:06:19,977 --> 00:06:21,187
Goodbye.

76
00:06:21,353 --> 00:06:22,438
Bye.

77
00:06:46,462 --> 00:06:47,922
So there it is.

78
00:06:48,088 --> 00:06:49,882
Meanwhile City.

79
00:06:51,217 --> 00:06:53,219
So beautiful from the upper heights...

80
00:06:53,385 --> 00:06:56,222
it almost looks like
it makes some kind of sense.

81
00:06:57,097 --> 00:07:01,310
From a distance, you'd never think
this city was hopelessly insane.

82
00:07:03,813 --> 00:07:05,105
It seems so long ago

83
00:07:05,272 --> 00:07:09,151
that the clockwork of events
that led me here began to turn.

84
00:07:09,318 --> 00:07:11,278
Events that led me to this room,

85
00:07:11,445 --> 00:07:14,156
to the task that I have
to perform tonight -

86
00:07:14,323 --> 00:07:17,368
the eradication of The Individual.

87
00:07:20,579 --> 00:07:23,040
Back then, things seemed so simple.

88
00:07:23,207 --> 00:07:25,626
It seemed like any other job,

89
00:07:25,835 --> 00:07:28,295
any other night
on the streets downtown.

90
00:07:28,462 --> 00:07:31,966
The main drag
was swarming with the faithful.

91
00:07:58,826 --> 00:08:01,245
..open mind and a steadfast faith

92
00:08:01,412 --> 00:08:03,664
applies the unchanging values
of our religion

93
00:08:03,873 --> 00:08:06,500
to the new priorities
of the people of Meanwhile City.

94
00:08:06,625 --> 00:08:11,172
Our plan - to improve your lives,
to provide opportunity...

95
00:08:11,338 --> 00:08:15,301
We are all immortal, spiritual beings.

96
00:08:21,056 --> 00:08:24,018
I didn't like using
the main thoroughfares.

97
00:08:24,560 --> 00:08:26,896
The Ministry clerics
were always out in force.

98
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:31,442
You see, you've got to have religion
to live in Meanwhile City.

99
00:08:33,569 --> 00:08:35,613
It's the law.

100
00:08:43,579 --> 00:08:46,582
There are now so many faiths
registered in this town,

101
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:49,001
it gets kind of hard to be original.

102
00:08:49,168 --> 00:08:52,254
..find yourself clean on the outside...

103
00:08:52,421 --> 00:08:54,465
..the water has been drained.

104
00:08:55,466 --> 00:08:57,510
Objects such as coins,

105
00:08:57,635 --> 00:08:59,595
safety pins, stones,

106
00:08:59,804 --> 00:09:04,266
cause extensive damage
and must not be placed in the machine.

107
00:09:04,433 --> 00:09:06,310
These days,
you can form a congregation

108
00:09:06,477 --> 00:09:09,104
simply based
on washing-machine instructions.

109
00:09:10,147 --> 00:09:14,068
Always consult the care instructions
on the clothes.

110
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:26,789
You see, without faith,
it's difficult to be controlled.

111
00:09:26,956 --> 00:09:29,166
And I didn't like being controlled.

112
00:09:29,333 --> 00:09:31,794
Not by anybody.

113
00:09:31,961 --> 00:09:34,046
That made me a big problem
for the Ministry.

114
00:09:34,213 --> 00:09:36,465
I'm the one and only non-believer

115
00:09:36,632 --> 00:09:38,300
in Meanwhile City.

116
00:09:42,638 --> 00:09:46,100
I'd been investigating a nasty
little faith known as Duplex Ride.

117
00:09:46,267 --> 00:09:50,020
Their leader called himself
The Individual.

118
00:09:50,187 --> 00:09:53,440
He was one of the most dangerous
I'd come across.

119
00:09:54,650 --> 00:09:58,028
Egocentric and insanely deluded.

120
00:10:00,990 --> 00:10:04,034
The Individual had abducted a young girl
into Duplex Ride.

121
00:10:05,202 --> 00:10:06,787
For what purpose?

122
00:10:06,954 --> 00:10:08,789
Somebody's god only knew.

123
00:10:12,793 --> 00:10:14,170
God bless you.

124
00:10:16,213 --> 00:10:17,840
How's tricks?

125
00:10:19,425 --> 00:10:21,177
Whisky, please.

126
00:10:21,343 --> 00:10:23,471
- Straight.
- Coming up.

127
00:10:25,973 --> 00:10:27,975
Hot outside today.

128
00:10:34,106 --> 00:10:35,483
He here?

129
00:10:37,443 --> 00:10:39,487
You're sure you wanna stay
for this drink?

130
00:10:39,653 --> 00:10:40,863
Think I shouldn't?

131
00:10:41,030 --> 00:10:42,823
He's in the back.

132
00:10:51,874 --> 00:10:53,459
- Thanks.
- No problem.

133
00:10:54,627 --> 00:10:56,128
Your god bless you.

134
00:10:58,756 --> 00:11:02,718
Wormsnakes -
my eyes and ears on the street.

135
00:11:02,885 --> 00:11:04,303
Ha, ha!

136
00:11:04,470 --> 00:11:05,805
Mr Preest!

137
00:11:07,056 --> 00:11:08,599
Looking...

138
00:11:08,766 --> 00:11:10,434
You're looking well.

139
00:11:10,601 --> 00:11:12,895
You know how I feel
about public appearances.

140
00:11:13,062 --> 00:11:14,980
Just tell me what you got.

141
00:11:15,147 --> 00:11:18,818
Mr Preest, information...
is very hard to come by these days,

142
00:11:18,984 --> 00:11:22,112
let alone having any faith in it,
you know what I mean?

143
00:11:22,279 --> 00:11:23,656
Snakes,

144
00:11:23,781 --> 00:11:25,616
I'm running out of patience.

145
00:11:25,783 --> 00:11:27,785
You don't understand!

146
00:11:29,453 --> 00:11:31,789
If he finds out that I...

147
00:11:31,956 --> 00:11:35,167
It'll be nothing to what
I'll do if you don't.

148
00:11:35,334 --> 00:11:36,877
The girl, Snakes!

149
00:11:37,044 --> 00:11:38,629
Where is she?

150
00:11:39,421 --> 00:11:41,632
The girl, she's dead.

151
00:11:42,633 --> 00:11:44,635
- Please!
- The Individual?

152
00:11:44,802 --> 00:11:47,096
I don't know! I swear, I don't know!

153
00:11:47,263 --> 00:11:50,641
- Did he do it himself?
- I don't know the...the d-d-details.

154
00:11:50,808 --> 00:11:54,478
You know, she didn't...didn't suffer.
That's all I know.

155
00:11:54,645 --> 00:11:58,190
- Just tell me where he is.
- I don't know! I swear!

156
00:11:58,357 --> 00:12:01,861
All I know is that you should
get out of here before they...

157
00:12:02,027 --> 00:12:04,113
Before what?

158
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:06,073
Ssh! They made me.

159
00:12:09,618 --> 00:12:10,953
No! No!

160
00:12:12,329 --> 00:12:14,165
I'll be back for you.

161
00:12:34,018 --> 00:12:36,520
Too many clerics on the street.

162
00:12:36,687 --> 00:12:38,647
I should have seen the signs.

163
00:12:38,814 --> 00:12:40,316
Stupid.

164
00:12:47,948 --> 00:12:50,659
- Just like that?
- Just like that.

165
00:12:53,037 --> 00:12:54,914
Are you sure?

166
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:57,666
I mean, you guys have been
down this road before.

167
00:12:57,833 --> 00:13:00,294
That's just it.
Maybe I should have seen it coming.

168
00:13:01,879 --> 00:13:05,049
Does being jilted at the altar count
when it's your rehearsal day?

169
00:13:05,216 --> 00:13:06,300
Milo.

170
00:13:06,467 --> 00:13:07,468
Come on.

171
00:13:07,635 --> 00:13:09,386
Just a thought.

172
00:13:10,846 --> 00:13:12,973
There's so many people to call.

173
00:13:13,891 --> 00:13:15,684
Do you think she's spoken to anyone?

174
00:13:15,851 --> 00:13:18,479
That's the last thing
you should be thinking about.

175
00:13:20,481 --> 00:13:22,691
It's hard enough
bloody organising a wedding.

176
00:13:22,858 --> 00:13:24,985
How the fuck do you go about
dismantling one?

177
00:13:25,152 --> 00:13:27,947
- They don't tell you that, do they?
- Just relax.

178
00:13:28,113 --> 00:13:29,824
I'll take care of everything.

179
00:13:30,825 --> 00:13:32,576
I'm still your best man, OK?

180
00:13:32,785 --> 00:13:34,453
It's my duty, right?

181
00:13:41,627 --> 00:13:43,295
Do you need to stay tonight?

182
00:13:43,462 --> 00:13:45,381
No, I'll probably just head back to mine.

183
00:13:45,548 --> 00:13:48,175
All right, just thought
you might like the company.

184
00:13:55,099 --> 00:13:57,017
Mate.

185
00:15:09,632 --> 00:15:12,802
This is Emilia. Leave a message.

186
00:15:13,886 --> 00:15:15,471
Emilia? Hello?

187
00:15:15,638 --> 00:15:18,599
Er, Emilia,
it's Gavin Clunes from college.

188
00:15:18,808 --> 00:15:20,643
I've not seen you in for a while.

189
00:15:20,851 --> 00:15:23,979
I don't need to remind you
that your deadline was Thursday.

190
00:15:24,146 --> 00:15:25,981
Call me back if you can.

191
00:15:30,277 --> 00:15:33,113
She was lost, needed my help.

192
00:15:34,198 --> 00:15:36,200
And I'd let her down.

193
00:15:36,367 --> 00:15:39,578
A routine cult job,

194
00:15:39,787 --> 00:15:42,414
and now the girl I was supposed to save
was dead.

195
00:15:42,581 --> 00:15:44,834
The Individual had gone to ground

196
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,670
and Wormsnakes had given me up
to the Ministry.

197
00:15:57,012 --> 00:15:59,098
I knew I was a wanted man.

198
00:15:59,265 --> 00:16:01,600
But even I hadn't expected
that much attention.

199
00:16:42,141 --> 00:16:44,977
Well, let's see what
all the fuss is about.

200
00:16:47,438 --> 00:16:50,983
Somebody upstairs had wanted me
brought in. And whoever they were...

201
00:16:52,568 --> 00:16:54,820
..they were good.

202
00:17:04,997 --> 00:17:06,540
Shit.

203
00:17:18,636 --> 00:17:21,555
Anywhere can feel like a prison
when you don't have any faith.

204
00:17:31,607 --> 00:17:34,443
The only thing that got me through
the endless night...

205
00:17:35,444 --> 00:17:37,112
..was to plan,

206
00:17:37,279 --> 00:17:39,073
stay focused...

207
00:17:40,991 --> 00:17:42,493
..stay sane.

208
00:17:47,832 --> 00:17:49,333
Then, out of nowhere,

209
00:17:49,500 --> 00:17:51,126
they came.

210
00:18:05,141 --> 00:18:06,851
Slowly now...

211
00:18:07,017 --> 00:18:08,519
Get up.

212
00:18:30,708 --> 00:18:32,209
Tarrant.

213
00:18:33,210 --> 00:18:36,255
The nearest I ever got
to the face behind the curtain.

214
00:18:38,048 --> 00:18:40,009
Nice to see you again, John.

215
00:18:40,176 --> 00:18:42,511
Yesterday, we received word

216
00:18:42,636 --> 00:18:45,598
that one of our stations in
the South City had been hit.

217
00:18:46,682 --> 00:18:48,559
Chemical attack of some kind.

218
00:18:49,393 --> 00:18:50,686
All operatives lost,

219
00:18:50,895 --> 00:18:53,814
as well as any hope of monitoring
the southern wall.

220
00:18:54,815 --> 00:18:56,442
It wasn't me.

221
00:18:58,110 --> 00:18:59,487
Quite.

222
00:19:00,821 --> 00:19:02,823
However, we do know who it was.

223
00:19:02,990 --> 00:19:06,202
Consequently, we have a proposition
to put to you...

224
00:19:07,203 --> 00:19:11,457
You lock me up for four years and now,
all of a sudden, you want to...

225
00:19:11,624 --> 00:19:13,125
Offer you a job.

226
00:19:13,250 --> 00:19:14,460
Interested?

227
00:19:14,627 --> 00:19:17,046
What could possibly interest me?

228
00:19:17,213 --> 00:19:18,631
Freedom, perhaps.

229
00:19:18,839 --> 00:19:21,759
The chance to settle an old score.

230
00:19:24,261 --> 00:19:27,223
Familiar faces have been turning up
in Meanwhile City,

231
00:19:27,348 --> 00:19:31,477
every one of them a fully-fledged,
paid-up member of...

232
00:19:32,228 --> 00:19:34,271
..Duplex Ride.

233
00:19:35,606 --> 00:19:37,066
That's right.

234
00:19:37,233 --> 00:19:40,069
The nasty little religion
that murdered your last client.

235
00:19:46,951 --> 00:19:49,829
"Life through the eyes
of the sole beholder.

236
00:19:49,995 --> 00:19:53,666
The world around him tailored
and designed for the one and only..."

237
00:19:53,874 --> 00:19:56,252
- The Individual.
- That's right.

238
00:19:56,377 --> 00:19:59,296
Seems like your old nemesis
is finally coming home to roost.

239
00:19:59,463 --> 00:20:01,966
We want to give you
a chance to make amends.

240
00:20:02,133 --> 00:20:03,717
For what?

241
00:20:04,635 --> 00:20:06,804
You're a man without religion, John,

242
00:20:06,971 --> 00:20:08,806
a man without direction.

243
00:20:09,807 --> 00:20:12,393
We want you to come to peace
with your inner self,

244
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:15,604
embrace a belief, however small.

245
00:20:17,940 --> 00:20:19,733
How old was she, John?

246
00:20:20,609 --> 00:20:23,404
How old was the little girl
you failed to save?

247
00:20:23,571 --> 00:20:25,739
10? 11?

248
00:20:27,825 --> 00:20:29,243
Count yourself lucky

249
00:20:29,368 --> 00:20:33,164
that absolution is very much part
of this religion's dogma.

250
00:20:33,289 --> 00:20:36,208
The Individual is coming back
to Meanwhile City.

251
00:20:37,376 --> 00:20:38,419
So?

252
00:20:38,586 --> 00:20:41,464
Well, you'll be doing us all a service.

253
00:20:42,298 --> 00:20:44,258
You'll have the Ministry's permission,

254
00:20:44,383 --> 00:20:46,177
sectarian permission,

255
00:20:46,302 --> 00:20:48,387
to commit this sin.

256
00:20:48,554 --> 00:20:50,806
Can I assume you're going to cooperate?

257
00:20:55,144 --> 00:20:57,146
So what happens now?

258
00:20:57,313 --> 00:20:59,440
Good. No time like the present.

259
00:20:59,607 --> 00:21:03,319
Take him to the hospital,
get him dressed and field ready, please.

260
00:21:05,738 --> 00:21:07,072
Oh, and, John...

261
00:21:07,239 --> 00:21:10,075
You'll probably be needing this.

262
00:23:14,074 --> 00:23:15,826
She went out the back.

263
00:23:17,203 --> 00:23:19,163
You won't see her today.

264
00:23:19,955 --> 00:23:21,832
"Her"?

265
00:24:25,229 --> 00:24:28,691
My name is Emilia Bryant.

266
00:24:28,899 --> 00:24:30,818
And I'm a liar.

267
00:24:32,486 --> 00:24:33,821
Drowning in depression

268
00:24:33,988 --> 00:24:36,699
at the bottomless lake
of my fathomless mind,

269
00:24:36,907 --> 00:24:38,909
a mind that's lost its heart.

270
00:24:40,452 --> 00:24:41,996
Disappointing, isn't it?

271
00:24:44,790 --> 00:24:47,126
Come closer, beautiful girl.

272
00:24:47,293 --> 00:24:49,920
I want to fall into
the depth of your eyes,

273
00:24:50,087 --> 00:24:53,883
kiss your lips as red as blood.

274
00:24:56,469 --> 00:24:58,220
We understand one another.

275
00:25:08,272 --> 00:25:11,150
Emergency services.
Which service do you require?

276
00:25:11,317 --> 00:25:12,568
Ambulance.

277
00:25:12,693 --> 00:25:15,821
74 Leonard Street, London EC2.

278
00:25:15,988 --> 00:25:17,156
Flat 3.

279
00:25:17,323 --> 00:25:20,075
OK. Can you tell me
what the problem is there?

280
00:25:21,160 --> 00:25:24,038
Suicide attempt. Hurry.

281
00:26:09,625 --> 00:26:12,419
Next stop, Meanwhile City Hospital.

282
00:26:13,879 --> 00:26:17,341
Not many people left this place
in better shape than they arrived.

283
00:26:17,508 --> 00:26:19,468
I knew why I was there.

284
00:26:19,635 --> 00:26:22,263
And I was running out of time.

285
00:26:31,647 --> 00:26:32,857
Here.

286
00:26:34,024 --> 00:26:35,401
Get in!

287
00:26:42,783 --> 00:26:44,660
Oh, hello, dear.

288
00:26:46,662 --> 00:26:50,958
As Mr Tarrant probably explained,
we want to fix you up with a homing device.

289
00:26:51,125 --> 00:26:54,462
We don't want to lose track of you
on the streets, now, do we?

290
00:26:54,628 --> 00:26:57,256
Well, funnily enough,
he didn't mention it.

291
00:26:57,423 --> 00:27:00,134
I thought this was just a medical.

292
00:27:00,301 --> 00:27:01,677
Just a precaution.

293
00:27:01,844 --> 00:27:04,847
If you pop yourself on this chair,
I think we can do it with a local.

294
00:27:06,474 --> 00:27:08,392
Regulation for all clerics in the field.

295
00:27:10,519 --> 00:27:14,148
Come, now.
Not scared of a little procedure, are we?

296
00:28:03,364 --> 00:28:07,368
I needed to go to ground,
hit the safe house and make ready.

297
00:28:09,119 --> 00:28:11,580
I'd always intended
on dealing with The Individual

298
00:28:11,747 --> 00:28:13,916
in my own way.

299
00:28:23,759 --> 00:28:25,636
How long since the call?

300
00:28:25,803 --> 00:28:29,098
- 14, 15 minutes.
- Come on, love. Wake up now!

301
00:28:35,187 --> 00:28:37,189
Give her some oxygen.

302
00:28:41,902 --> 00:28:43,779
Who is she?

303
00:28:43,946 --> 00:28:47,783
Name - Emilia Bryant.
Next of kin - Margaret Bryant. Blood type A.

304
00:28:47,908 --> 00:28:50,119
Emilia, come on, wake up now.

305
00:28:50,286 --> 00:28:51,954
Wake up, love.

306
00:28:52,121 --> 00:28:53,289
Emilia?

307
00:28:53,455 --> 00:28:55,291
Emilia, can you hear me?

308
00:28:57,793 --> 00:28:59,628
Let's move her.

309
00:29:00,588 --> 00:29:03,424
OK, Steve, prep Thomas's.
Tell them we've got an OD.

310
00:29:03,591 --> 00:29:05,968
One, two, three...

311
00:29:31,744 --> 00:29:34,872
Young female, mid-twenties,
found unconscious on her bed.

312
00:29:35,039 --> 00:29:38,709
Left a suicide note, by the looks of it.
All the details are there for us.

313
00:29:38,876 --> 00:29:40,669
Baseline obs look pretty good.

314
00:29:40,836 --> 00:29:43,839
- But otherwise not much response.
- OK, one minute.

315
00:29:44,882 --> 00:29:47,259
- One minute.
- Put her in room six.

316
00:29:47,426 --> 00:29:50,304
- Are you OK?
- It's been a crazy week.

317
00:29:53,224 --> 00:29:54,642
Number six again.

318
00:30:05,820 --> 00:30:08,489
Today on Radio 4 with
John Humphreys and Edward Stone.

319
00:30:08,656 --> 00:30:10,658
Hello?

320
00:30:11,742 --> 00:30:12,952
Yes?

321
00:30:15,037 --> 00:30:16,455
Oh, yes?

322
00:30:20,084 --> 00:30:21,627
Oh, my God.

323
00:30:23,504 --> 00:30:25,840
No, no, no, he hasn't been here.

324
00:30:27,466 --> 00:30:29,927
What do you mean,
has he contacted me? Where is he?

325
00:30:32,221 --> 00:30:34,056
Um...yes.

326
00:30:34,223 --> 00:30:37,643
Well, you'll...you'll call me back.
You'll call me back when?

327
00:30:39,478 --> 00:30:40,813
Well...

328
00:30:40,938 --> 00:30:42,857
Well, of course.

329
00:30:47,987 --> 00:30:50,281
Yes. Yes, I will.

330
00:30:50,447 --> 00:30:53,200
I'm very sorry. Goodbye.

331
00:33:29,231 --> 00:33:30,941
No, I'm sorry.

332
00:33:33,444 --> 00:33:35,988
I tell you what,
these are the last names...

333
00:33:54,089 --> 00:33:55,674
Did you call my mother?

334
00:33:55,883 --> 00:33:56,926
Hm?

335
00:33:58,844 --> 00:34:00,638
Did you call my mother?

336
00:34:00,846 --> 00:34:02,056
Yes.

337
00:34:02,181 --> 00:34:04,099
The staff nurse spoke to her.

338
00:34:06,352 --> 00:34:08,437
Let me guess.

339
00:34:08,604 --> 00:34:10,564
She wanted to know if you were OK.

340
00:34:12,149 --> 00:34:13,901
But not enough to come down here.

341
00:34:14,068 --> 00:34:15,194
Right?

342
00:34:31,210 --> 00:34:32,670
I'm sorry.

343
00:34:32,878 --> 00:34:35,256
- Would you like me to...?
- No, no, no.

344
00:34:35,422 --> 00:34:37,883
That's all right. Please carry on.

345
00:34:42,138 --> 00:34:44,390
I look after a church myself.

346
00:34:45,808 --> 00:34:47,351
I'm a warden.

347
00:34:49,186 --> 00:34:51,188
Back in Cambridge.

348
00:34:56,068 --> 00:34:58,070
It never stops, does it?

349
00:34:59,113 --> 00:35:00,698
It's the same.

350
00:35:03,200 --> 00:35:04,201
Actually...

351
00:35:05,202 --> 00:35:07,204
I'm here looking for somebody.

352
00:35:08,581 --> 00:35:10,291
My son.

353
00:35:10,458 --> 00:35:12,084
Would you...?

354
00:35:16,255 --> 00:35:17,631
I don't know.

355
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:19,967
I see so many here. Every day.

356
00:35:20,134 --> 00:35:21,719
I can imagine.

357
00:35:27,558 --> 00:35:28,434
What?

358
00:35:28,601 --> 00:35:29,977
What is it?

359
00:35:30,144 --> 00:35:31,604
He is lost.

360
00:35:33,022 --> 00:35:34,315
Yes, he is.

361
00:35:34,482 --> 00:35:36,484
That's why I'm looking for him.

362
00:35:41,447 --> 00:35:42,948
Could I...?

363
00:35:44,241 --> 00:35:45,242
Please.

364
00:35:47,578 --> 00:35:49,079
I'm sorry.

365
00:35:49,205 --> 00:35:51,207
I haven't seen this person.

366
00:35:52,833 --> 00:35:54,835
That's all right. Thank you, anyway.

367
00:36:04,220 --> 00:36:05,888
If you needed to find someone,

368
00:36:06,055 --> 00:36:09,266
the best place to start
was the Faith Registration Centre -

369
00:36:10,351 --> 00:36:12,478
Meanwhile's melting pot of the pious.

370
00:36:17,525 --> 00:36:20,069
Every creed, cult, religion and doctrine

371
00:36:20,236 --> 00:36:21,779
pass through these doors,

372
00:36:21,946 --> 00:36:24,949
all looking for the same sense
of belonging and hope.

373
00:36:28,953 --> 00:36:32,414
I just hoped that Wormsnakes
had managed to hold onto his job.

374
00:36:36,335 --> 00:36:37,336
Next!

375
00:36:44,802 --> 00:36:46,053
He's in there.

376
00:36:50,391 --> 00:36:52,268
Nothing had changed.

377
00:36:52,434 --> 00:36:55,855
This was still a living,
breathing testament to the insanity

378
00:36:56,021 --> 00:36:57,731
of the Ministry's grip on this city.

379
00:37:02,528 --> 00:37:04,280
Please be advised that queue-jumping...

380
00:37:04,446 --> 00:37:10,161
A free blessing
for every donation we receive.

381
00:37:11,328 --> 00:37:12,538
Hi, I'm Teri. How can I help?

382
00:37:12,705 --> 00:37:15,207
I'm looking for somebody
who works in the kitchen.

383
00:37:15,332 --> 00:37:18,127
Oh, OK. I just need you
to enter your faith for the record.

384
00:37:18,294 --> 00:37:20,171
- Why?
- For the register.

385
00:37:20,296 --> 00:37:21,922
What's your faith?

386
00:37:22,089 --> 00:37:23,424
What's yours?

387
00:37:23,591 --> 00:37:27,928
Well, at the moment, I'm with
some Seventh Day Manicurists.

388
00:37:29,472 --> 00:37:30,890
But I'm thinking of changing.

389
00:37:31,056 --> 00:37:34,560
The level of discussion isn't great
and we've nearly run out of colours.

390
00:37:35,478 --> 00:37:38,147
It's probably not your thing.
If you just want to sign in.

391
00:37:39,273 --> 00:37:41,734
Thank you. I've seen all I need to see.

392
00:37:41,901 --> 00:37:43,736
OK. Don't mention it and God bless you.

393
00:37:46,155 --> 00:37:48,157
Hi, I'm Teri. How can I help?

394
00:38:09,220 --> 00:38:11,222
You're not allowed to smoke in here.

395
00:38:13,516 --> 00:38:15,518
Do you think?

396
00:38:19,522 --> 00:38:21,524
I saw you come in. Last night.

397
00:38:23,234 --> 00:38:25,069
May I talk to you for a moment?

398
00:38:25,236 --> 00:38:26,612
I can...

399
00:38:27,738 --> 00:38:29,740
..buy you a hot drink.

400
00:38:31,742 --> 00:38:32,701
Please.

401
00:38:41,293 --> 00:38:43,295
We get many suicides.

402
00:38:44,380 --> 00:38:45,381
Oh.

403
00:38:48,634 --> 00:38:50,636
I heard the paramedics talking.

404
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:53,722
So you know the whole story.

405
00:38:54,682 --> 00:38:56,976
My name is Pastor Bone.

406
00:38:57,143 --> 00:38:59,854
It means "bread of life".

407
00:39:00,020 --> 00:39:01,897
Look, Mr...whoever you are,

408
00:39:02,064 --> 00:39:04,400
- I appreciate...
- I knew someone once.

409
00:39:06,610 --> 00:39:10,156
She did what you tried to do last night.

410
00:39:11,448 --> 00:39:13,450
She was...successful.

411
00:39:14,535 --> 00:39:16,412
She started a chain of events like...

412
00:39:16,579 --> 00:39:17,746
dominoes.

413
00:39:17,913 --> 00:39:19,582
I'm sorry, but I really should...

414
00:39:19,790 --> 00:39:23,169
I'm just saying that it isn't just about
your family, your friends,

415
00:39:23,335 --> 00:39:24,837
the people you leave behind.

416
00:39:25,004 --> 00:39:27,756
It's about the people
you haven't met yet.

417
00:39:31,260 --> 00:39:33,512
A person can stay inside themselves
for too long

418
00:39:33,721 --> 00:39:37,516
and end up blind, like not recognising
your own voice on tape or...

419
00:39:37,725 --> 00:39:39,351
It's an art project.

420
00:39:41,061 --> 00:39:42,605
- I'm sorry. I...
- Listen.

421
00:39:43,898 --> 00:39:44,690
I...

422
00:39:44,899 --> 00:39:47,067
I get to piss off my mother
and my tutors.

423
00:39:47,234 --> 00:39:49,820
I get to kill myself every month
without dying.

424
00:39:49,987 --> 00:39:51,655
I'm having a ball.

425
00:39:51,864 --> 00:39:53,073
OK?

426
00:39:56,827 --> 00:39:58,829
You know what, Mr Bone?

427
00:40:00,247 --> 00:40:03,042
You should get yourself a job
as a social worker here.

428
00:40:06,837 --> 00:40:07,963
Thank you.

429
00:40:08,130 --> 00:40:09,715
For the coffee.

430
00:40:37,743 --> 00:40:40,454
I followed Wormsnakes home
after his shift.

431
00:40:40,579 --> 00:40:44,208
Snakes' neighbourhood suited
his personality down to a T.

432
00:40:45,209 --> 00:40:46,627
Fractured. Infected.

433
00:40:46,836 --> 00:40:48,045
Forgotten.

434
00:40:49,088 --> 00:40:51,090
Meanwhile's slum quarter.

435
00:41:16,031 --> 00:41:17,116
Jesus Christ!

436
00:41:17,283 --> 00:41:19,118
Wormsnakes.

437
00:41:20,536 --> 00:41:22,538
Get the fuck out of my apartment now!

438
00:41:23,581 --> 00:41:25,416
Let's not make this difficult.

439
00:41:26,542 --> 00:41:28,419
What do you want from me?

440
00:41:28,544 --> 00:41:30,296
What do you want?

441
00:41:33,048 --> 00:41:34,633
You're crazy. Know that, yeah?

442
00:41:38,137 --> 00:41:40,181
Be polite.
You owe me, remember?

443
00:41:40,347 --> 00:41:43,559
For every single day of my four years.

444
00:41:43,726 --> 00:41:45,352
My fucking nose!

445
00:41:47,062 --> 00:41:51,233
Now, then, the word on the street is
The Individual is coming to town.

446
00:41:52,318 --> 00:41:55,571
You wouldn't happen to know anything
about that, now, would you?

447
00:41:55,738 --> 00:41:57,323
No! No! I swear.

448
00:41:58,073 --> 00:41:59,492
Uhh...

449
00:42:00,576 --> 00:42:02,411
I don't believe you.

450
00:42:03,871 --> 00:42:05,998
I need you to do a little favour for me.

451
00:42:09,335 --> 00:42:12,421
I want you to tell The Individual
where he can find me.

452
00:42:12,588 --> 00:42:13,714
How do you know...

453
00:42:13,881 --> 00:42:15,758
How do you know he is gonna come
and find me?

454
00:42:15,925 --> 00:42:17,510
I found you, didn't I?

455
00:42:18,511 --> 00:42:20,304
I'm gonna be at this address.

456
00:42:21,722 --> 00:42:23,724
And rest assured, he'll find you.

457
00:42:25,434 --> 00:42:26,894
Just do your job.

458
00:42:27,061 --> 00:42:28,896
What little faith I have...

459
00:42:29,939 --> 00:42:31,565
..I have it in you.

460
00:42:35,611 --> 00:42:37,613
You're a lucky man, Snakes.

461
00:42:39,073 --> 00:42:41,033
You've got a stay of execution.

462
00:42:42,201 --> 00:42:43,494
Understand?

463
00:42:44,620 --> 00:42:46,622
I'll be waiting and watching.

464
00:42:49,625 --> 00:42:51,335
Nice to see you again.

465
00:42:53,337 --> 00:42:55,214
Fucking likewise, I'm sure.

466
00:42:55,381 --> 00:42:58,384
I knew he'd deliver my message
one way or another.

467
00:42:59,885 --> 00:43:01,470
Now all I had to do...

468
00:43:01,637 --> 00:43:03,097
was wait.

469
00:43:05,307 --> 00:43:08,310
So another in a long line of
relationships bites the dust.

470
00:43:09,311 --> 00:43:13,732
And after all this...experience,
the same thing happening again and again,

471
00:43:13,899 --> 00:43:15,776
I understand it all even less.

472
00:43:15,943 --> 00:43:17,236
Cheers.

473
00:43:17,403 --> 00:43:19,613
- Cheers.
- Hey. Hey. What did I say?

474
00:43:22,491 --> 00:43:25,619
- Spoilsport.
- Whatever the subject, let's change it.

475
00:43:26,662 --> 00:43:28,205
How about this?

476
00:43:29,206 --> 00:43:31,041
I think I saw Sally again.

477
00:43:31,208 --> 00:43:32,543
Yesterday.

478
00:43:32,668 --> 00:43:36,881
This again? Technically, that's not
really changing the subject, is it?

479
00:43:37,047 --> 00:43:39,717
- Who's Sally?
- Milo's childhood sweetheart.

480
00:43:40,676 --> 00:43:43,095
I think I saw her
around a couple of months ago.

481
00:43:43,262 --> 00:43:45,514
It felt like she was following me
or something.

482
00:43:45,681 --> 00:43:47,933
This time, it was closer.
I'm sure it was her.

483
00:43:48,100 --> 00:43:50,769
- Childhood sweetheart?
- When I was about seven.

484
00:43:50,936 --> 00:43:52,313
See what I mean?

485
00:43:52,480 --> 00:43:54,982
I think that's lovely.
See? Romance is not dead.

486
00:43:55,149 --> 00:43:57,443
Come on.
Enough of the romantic bullshit.

487
00:43:57,610 --> 00:44:00,488
- Thank you very much.
- Do you see what you're doing to me?

488
00:44:01,322 --> 00:44:03,324
Oh...

489
00:44:30,017 --> 00:44:33,729
I heard this story once
when I was a kid, or read it.

490
00:44:33,896 --> 00:44:35,523
It was about a storyteller

491
00:44:35,689 --> 00:44:40,444
who was so good at telling stories
that everything he made up became real.

492
00:44:40,778 --> 00:44:42,655
Which would be an awesome superpower.

493
00:44:42,822 --> 00:44:44,865
Exactly.

494
00:44:45,032 --> 00:44:47,660
So the storyteller creates
a world for himself

495
00:44:47,827 --> 00:44:51,413
where he's the king of the castle,
has a beautiful princess on his arm.

496
00:44:51,580 --> 00:44:54,291
- The sun's-always-shining kind of stuff.
- Yeah?

497
00:44:56,502 --> 00:44:58,504
And then, one day, he wakes up.

498
00:44:59,880 --> 00:45:01,340
He looks around.

499
00:45:01,507 --> 00:45:03,509
He kisses her on the cheek and...

500
00:45:04,593 --> 00:45:05,928
..legs it.

501
00:45:06,095 --> 00:45:07,304
Why?

502
00:45:08,222 --> 00:45:09,682
I don't know.

503
00:45:11,016 --> 00:45:13,978
Even though his life was perfect,
absolutely perfect,

504
00:45:14,145 --> 00:45:16,730
he had the feeling he should be
somewhere else.

505
00:45:16,897 --> 00:45:18,691
With someone else.

506
00:45:20,526 --> 00:45:23,028
Anyway, the princess wakes up
and he's gone.

507
00:45:25,030 --> 00:45:27,032
And that's it. I guess.

508
00:45:28,033 --> 00:45:30,035
Does that make any sense?

509
00:45:34,206 --> 00:45:35,291
No.

510
00:45:36,208 --> 00:45:38,210
I'm going to open another bottle.

511
00:46:22,838 --> 00:46:24,715
I take it that's how it ends.

512
00:46:26,509 --> 00:46:28,677
It ends when you want
to stop watching it.

513
00:46:28,844 --> 00:46:30,679
Well, that happens to be right now.

514
00:46:41,273 --> 00:46:42,650
That was real.

515
00:46:42,858 --> 00:46:44,151
Define "real".

516
00:46:44,318 --> 00:46:46,195
You called the ambulance.

517
00:46:46,362 --> 00:46:48,781
I had to. I'd have died, otherwise.

518
00:46:48,906 --> 00:46:51,116
I can't let you submit this, Emilia.

519
00:46:51,283 --> 00:46:53,160
- You know that.
- You're censoring me?

520
00:46:53,327 --> 00:46:55,496
This is way more extreme
than the last one.

521
00:46:55,663 --> 00:46:57,123
It's not finished.

522
00:46:58,666 --> 00:47:01,001
What happened
to your Following project?

523
00:47:01,168 --> 00:47:05,506
Two months following random strangers
around London with your video camera.

524
00:47:05,673 --> 00:47:09,009
- Now you're going to throw it all away?
- The last guy saw me.

525
00:47:10,052 --> 00:47:13,931
I even wore a wig to disguise myself
for a few days, but it didn't work.

526
00:47:15,432 --> 00:47:16,725
It's over.

527
00:47:16,892 --> 00:47:18,352
So is this.

528
00:47:23,440 --> 00:47:26,443
I suggest you stop wasting
the emergency services' time.

529
00:47:26,610 --> 00:47:29,530
- Come up with something more original.
- More original?

530
00:47:29,738 --> 00:47:33,659
Shock and bad taste doesn't necessarily
equate with originality.

531
00:47:33,868 --> 00:47:36,912
Like I said, it's not finished.

532
00:47:37,037 --> 00:47:39,039
And how does it finish, Emilia?

533
00:47:40,040 --> 00:47:41,333
With you dead?

534
00:47:41,500 --> 00:47:43,085
The college sued?

535
00:47:46,464 --> 00:47:47,923
I don't know.

536
00:47:48,924 --> 00:47:50,551
Well, I bloody well do.

537
00:47:51,260 --> 00:47:52,720
Bin this drivel.

538
00:47:52,928 --> 00:47:54,472
Get back on track.

539
00:47:54,638 --> 00:47:56,640
Or don't bother coming back.

540
00:48:19,997 --> 00:48:23,083
When you're lost,
you're willing to believe anything.

541
00:48:24,084 --> 00:48:28,631
In this city, every religion promised a future,
whether in this world or the next.

542
00:48:29,632 --> 00:48:32,426
All you had to pay them with
was your faith and trust

543
00:48:32,593 --> 00:48:35,930
and, despite the celebration,
the reverence and the prayer,

544
00:48:36,055 --> 00:48:38,557
everybody ends up
in the same human mess.

545
00:48:38,724 --> 00:48:39,767
Old.

546
00:48:39,934 --> 00:48:40,976
Sick.

547
00:48:41,143 --> 00:48:42,311
Unhappy.

548
00:48:42,478 --> 00:48:43,729
Dead.

549
00:48:46,190 --> 00:48:47,650
She'd be 16 now.

550
00:48:47,858 --> 00:48:49,276
A young woman.

551
00:48:49,443 --> 00:48:51,403
The Individual had robbed her of life

552
00:48:51,570 --> 00:48:52,947
and, tonight,

553
00:48:53,072 --> 00:48:55,282
I was going to relieve him of his.

554
00:50:21,202 --> 00:50:23,078
You asked me how this finished.

555
00:50:23,204 --> 00:50:24,705
I told the truth.

556
00:50:24,914 --> 00:50:26,457
I don't know.

557
00:50:28,083 --> 00:50:29,919
A broken doll.

558
00:50:30,085 --> 00:50:31,545
A hollow girl.

559
00:50:31,754 --> 00:50:33,756
Bereft at the loss of her father.

560
00:50:35,841 --> 00:50:37,843
But part of me left when he did.

561
00:50:40,679 --> 00:50:44,058
Someone said, "It's about the people
you haven't met yet."

562
00:50:45,059 --> 00:50:46,936
Like the people on my tapes.

563
00:50:47,937 --> 00:50:49,939
I'm not sure I like the sound of them.

564
00:50:51,941 --> 00:50:53,192
The truth is...

565
00:50:53,359 --> 00:50:55,486
I'm a little scared
they might be like me.

566
00:50:58,697 --> 00:51:00,282
I'm sorry, Mr Clunes.

567
00:51:00,449 --> 00:51:02,451
That's the best I can do.

568
00:51:27,059 --> 00:51:28,644
Get me down!

569
00:51:46,412 --> 00:51:47,413
Hello.

570
00:51:48,497 --> 00:51:50,124
I was just...um...

571
00:51:51,167 --> 00:51:52,501
- Passing?
- Yeah.

572
00:51:53,502 --> 00:51:55,087
Sally.

573
00:51:55,212 --> 00:51:56,338
Wow.

574
00:51:56,505 --> 00:51:58,174
It must have been...

575
00:51:58,340 --> 00:52:00,301
- 20 years.
- 20 years, yeah.

576
00:52:00,468 --> 00:52:03,429
But...I saw you on the
street the other day.

577
00:52:03,596 --> 00:52:04,847
Oh.

578
00:52:05,598 --> 00:52:07,475
At least...I thought it was you.

579
00:52:07,641 --> 00:52:09,435
I got to thinking about you.

580
00:52:10,311 --> 00:52:11,896
Quite a lot, I guess.

581
00:52:12,897 --> 00:52:16,192
I just came to check the records.
I never thought you'd be working here.

582
00:52:17,193 --> 00:52:18,819
Check the records?

583
00:52:20,863 --> 00:52:23,616
Yeah, well, you know,
so I could try and contact you,

584
00:52:23,824 --> 00:52:25,659
write to you or something.

585
00:52:25,868 --> 00:52:28,204
Do you get a lunch hour?

586
00:52:29,497 --> 00:52:31,582
Can you spare a few minutes?

587
00:52:45,304 --> 00:52:46,806
Excuse me.

588
00:52:46,972 --> 00:52:49,266
Sorry. We're not really open yet.

589
00:52:49,433 --> 00:52:50,976
Er, yes, I know.

590
00:52:51,143 --> 00:52:52,561
I'm sorry, but...

591
00:52:52,770 --> 00:52:55,022
I was wondering if you could help me.

592
00:52:55,189 --> 00:52:57,191
I'm looking for someone.

593
00:53:00,319 --> 00:53:01,779
It's my son, you see.

594
00:53:02,446 --> 00:53:04,782
He used to come here
a few years ago and I...

595
00:53:04,949 --> 00:53:06,826
I just wondered if he'd been back.

596
00:53:06,992 --> 00:53:09,453
OK. Well, do you have a picture?
I can put it on the board.

597
00:53:09,620 --> 00:53:11,288
I do, actually.

598
00:53:11,455 --> 00:53:12,915
Erm...

599
00:53:13,082 --> 00:53:14,416
well, I only have this one.

600
00:53:14,583 --> 00:53:16,377
- It's OK. I can do a copy.
- Thank you.

601
00:53:21,715 --> 00:53:23,551
Do you recognise him?

602
00:53:23,759 --> 00:53:25,594
I don't know. Maybe.

603
00:53:26,595 --> 00:53:30,141
I couldn't say for sure.
He probably doesn't look like this any more.

604
00:53:32,143 --> 00:53:33,727
No, of course not.

605
00:53:35,479 --> 00:53:37,231
Look, I'm only part time.

606
00:53:37,982 --> 00:53:41,026
You could speak to Bill.
He's been here the longest. He'll be in later.

607
00:53:41,193 --> 00:53:42,653
Bill Wasnik.

608
00:53:43,779 --> 00:53:46,157
Why don't you
put your contact details on there?

609
00:53:46,282 --> 00:53:47,825
- Oh, yes.
- Do you have a pen?

610
00:53:47,992 --> 00:53:49,535
I do. Yes. Thank you.

611
00:53:58,711 --> 00:54:00,004
Great.

612
00:54:00,171 --> 00:54:01,630
Thanks.

613
00:54:32,787 --> 00:54:34,622
So when did you start teaching?

614
00:54:34,830 --> 00:54:36,373
- Pretty recently.
- Yeah?

615
00:54:38,292 --> 00:54:39,752
Suits you.

616
00:54:39,919 --> 00:54:41,253
Thank you.

617
00:54:41,378 --> 00:54:43,464
You look good with kids.

618
00:54:43,631 --> 00:54:45,633
You were always good with me.

619
00:54:46,759 --> 00:54:49,970
I know we were both kids at the time,
but you know what I mean.

620
00:54:50,137 --> 00:54:51,555
Yeah, I think so.

621
00:54:54,975 --> 00:54:56,393
How is your mum?

622
00:54:56,560 --> 00:54:57,436
OK.

623
00:54:57,603 --> 00:54:59,104
Still the same.

624
00:54:59,271 --> 00:55:01,065
Away with the fairies.

625
00:55:05,945 --> 00:55:07,947
When did you forget about me?

626
00:55:22,920 --> 00:55:24,046
- Hello.
- Anne.

627
00:55:24,213 --> 00:55:28,384
If you want to leave a message for Anne
or Martin, please speak after the tone.

628
00:55:39,770 --> 00:55:41,522
Well, I should get back.

629
00:55:42,606 --> 00:55:44,233
It's been really nice.

630
00:55:44,400 --> 00:55:46,277
Could I...see you again?

631
00:55:46,402 --> 00:55:47,486
Milo...

632
00:55:47,653 --> 00:55:49,530
We could go for a drink or something.

633
00:55:49,738 --> 00:55:53,659
- It's been so long, it's bizarre luck you...
- Yeah, but it's fate.

634
00:55:53,868 --> 00:55:56,454
Thought you didn't
believe in all that stuff.

635
00:55:56,620 --> 00:55:58,831
Look...
I'm not taking no for an answer.

636
00:55:58,998 --> 00:56:00,833
Any time at all. Any day this week.

637
00:56:01,000 --> 00:56:02,251
OK. OK.

638
00:56:02,418 --> 00:56:04,170
How about Friday?

639
00:56:04,336 --> 00:56:06,172
- Friday.
- All right.

640
00:56:06,338 --> 00:56:08,215
There's a... There's a restaurant.

641
00:56:08,382 --> 00:56:10,634
The Tabernacle.
On the corner of Lennox Street.

642
00:56:10,843 --> 00:56:12,845
- Yeah. I know it.
- Yeah?

643
00:56:13,012 --> 00:56:14,263
Eight?

644
00:56:14,430 --> 00:56:16,015
OK. I'll be there.

645
00:56:16,182 --> 00:56:18,017
Can I get your number?

646
00:56:18,184 --> 00:56:20,311
Everything OK? Can I help?

647
00:56:20,436 --> 00:56:22,438
No, it's fine, thanks. We're fine.

648
00:56:22,563 --> 00:56:24,773
- Don't expect too much.
- I won't.

649
00:56:24,940 --> 00:56:25,858
Friday.

650
00:56:39,038 --> 00:56:40,623
Her name was Sarah

651
00:56:40,831 --> 00:56:42,833
and she was only 11 years old.

652
00:56:44,001 --> 00:56:46,420
To The Individual and his twisted faith,

653
00:56:46,545 --> 00:56:48,631
she was just another soul sacrificed

654
00:56:48,839 --> 00:56:51,967
and forgotten in the detritus
of this senseless world.

655
00:56:53,469 --> 00:56:57,556
One little soul,
who is now about to be avenged.

656
00:57:04,021 --> 00:57:07,650
I had to keep it together, stay focused.

657
00:57:09,360 --> 00:57:10,986
It's nearly time.

658
00:57:16,367 --> 00:57:17,576
Hi, Mum.

659
00:57:21,622 --> 00:57:23,749
You could have come sooner, you know.

660
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:27,920
Might have seemed
a little bit too much like running away.

661
00:57:29,922 --> 00:57:32,508
Coming home is never like running away.

662
00:57:34,135 --> 00:57:36,011
What's happening with the flat?

663
00:57:36,178 --> 00:57:38,305
I might keep hold of
it for a while longer,

664
00:57:38,472 --> 00:57:41,851
but I'll probably spend a couple
of nights at Dan and Laura's.

665
00:57:42,017 --> 00:57:43,644
How is young Dan?

666
00:57:43,853 --> 00:57:48,607
A little embarrassed at his abject failure
as best man. Other than that, he's OK.

667
00:57:48,816 --> 00:57:49,650
Bless.

668
00:57:49,859 --> 00:57:51,527
It wasn't his fault.

669
00:57:55,364 --> 00:57:57,366
I think you've had a lucky escape.

670
00:58:32,234 --> 00:58:34,028
Bring her over here, please.

671
00:58:35,070 --> 00:58:37,072
She's bicardic.

672
00:58:37,823 --> 00:58:39,200
Get me some atropine.

673
00:58:48,417 --> 00:58:50,002
We're losing her.

674
00:59:07,812 --> 00:59:09,605
Er...Bill Wasnik?

675
00:59:11,482 --> 00:59:12,650
Yeah.

676
00:59:13,609 --> 00:59:15,778
Something kind of funny
has happened, though.

677
00:59:15,945 --> 00:59:17,530
Oh?

678
00:59:17,655 --> 00:59:19,365
I bumped into an old flame.

679
00:59:19,532 --> 00:59:21,408
Oh, really? Who?

680
00:59:21,575 --> 00:59:25,579
Do you remember Sally? She used to
come round after school sometimes.

681
00:59:29,959 --> 00:59:30,835
Sally?

682
00:59:31,001 --> 00:59:32,336
Yeah. Sally.

683
00:59:32,503 --> 00:59:35,589
I saw her this morning,
round the corner, at Boston Park.

684
00:59:35,756 --> 00:59:37,758
Which is weird.
She's teaching there now.

685
00:59:39,051 --> 00:59:41,262
We had a chat
and we're going to hook up.

686
00:59:45,516 --> 00:59:46,642
Milo.

687
00:59:46,851 --> 00:59:48,144
What?

688
00:59:50,354 --> 00:59:52,189
Karen must have hurt you so much.

689
00:59:52,356 --> 00:59:54,441
What's Karen got to do with this?

690
00:59:56,026 --> 00:59:58,696
How did it feel, seeing Sally again?

691
01:00:00,322 --> 01:00:01,323
Well...

692
01:00:02,324 --> 01:00:03,659
Good, actually.

693
01:00:03,826 --> 01:00:05,119
Nice.

694
01:00:07,329 --> 01:00:09,331
Kind of put things in perspective.

695
01:00:17,339 --> 01:00:19,175
What are you doing?

696
01:00:19,341 --> 01:00:21,343
I want to show you something.

697
01:00:33,814 --> 01:00:34,815
There.

698
01:00:36,525 --> 01:00:37,526
What?

699
01:00:37,693 --> 01:00:38,777
Sally.

700
01:00:38,903 --> 01:00:40,279
Where?

701
01:00:40,446 --> 01:00:41,655
Oh, Milo.

702
01:00:41,822 --> 01:00:43,741
What? I don't see her.

703
01:00:43,908 --> 01:00:48,037
When you were six,
she was in every photograph.

704
01:00:49,538 --> 01:00:51,624
What? What do you mean?

705
01:00:51,791 --> 01:00:53,667
After your father died,

706
01:00:53,834 --> 01:00:55,294
Sally turned up

707
01:00:55,461 --> 01:00:57,463
and kept you happy.

708
01:00:58,464 --> 01:00:59,965
I spoke to your teacher.

709
01:01:00,132 --> 01:01:03,677
She said it was normal for a child
of your age to have a friend like Sally.

710
01:01:03,844 --> 01:01:05,179
What? Sally wasn't...

711
01:01:05,346 --> 01:01:08,557
She appeared in our lives
right after your father died

712
01:01:08,724 --> 01:01:11,435
and disappeared
when you started to forget him.

713
01:01:12,520 --> 01:01:16,190
No.

714
01:01:16,357 --> 01:01:19,151
She's turned up in your time of need.

715
01:01:20,820 --> 01:01:22,530
I think it's quite sweet.

716
01:01:22,696 --> 01:01:26,158
No, no, no. No, I'm not getting involved
in any spooky bullshit.

717
01:01:26,325 --> 01:01:28,619
I saw her today. I spoke to her.

718
01:01:32,790 --> 01:01:36,168
All I ever get from you
is a load of half-arsed astrology.

719
01:01:36,335 --> 01:01:40,005
Whenever anything bad happens,
"Oh, well, it's meant to be."

720
01:01:41,799 --> 01:01:43,676
Well, I tell you, I saw this girl today.

721
01:01:43,843 --> 01:01:45,010
I saw her!

722
01:01:45,177 --> 01:01:48,347
And if it's not Sally,
then it's somebody pretending to be her.

723
01:01:57,481 --> 01:01:58,482
Jesus.

724
01:02:06,365 --> 01:02:09,994
I think you just don't realise
how unhappy you've been.

725
01:02:11,996 --> 01:02:12,997
Milo.

726
01:02:16,792 --> 01:02:19,545
The world is full of people
sent here to help us.

727
01:02:19,753 --> 01:02:21,922
Most of the time, we just don't see them.

728
01:02:23,549 --> 01:02:26,552
Whatever it was she wanted to say to you,
you should listen.

729
01:02:26,719 --> 01:02:30,097
Do you know what you're saying?
Do you actually know what you're saying?

730
01:02:30,264 --> 01:02:31,474
Milo.

731
01:02:34,143 --> 01:02:35,603
What's happening?

732
01:02:42,985 --> 01:02:45,237
You were a friend of David's?

733
01:02:45,404 --> 01:02:46,864
Not close.

734
01:02:47,031 --> 01:02:48,657
Army days.

735
01:02:49,784 --> 01:02:51,786
We was er...we was in Basra together.

736
01:02:52,828 --> 01:02:54,663
We met up again back here.

737
01:02:54,830 --> 01:02:56,665
Mostly at the centre.

738
01:02:58,250 --> 01:03:01,587
But er...I don't think Dave
would exactly count me as a mate.

739
01:03:05,633 --> 01:03:10,179
I'm not proud of it, Mr Esser,
but I led the filth...straight to him.

740
01:03:11,972 --> 01:03:15,476
We was in a pub, down at the market.

741
01:03:15,643 --> 01:03:17,520
Anyhow, he started freaking out.

742
01:03:17,686 --> 01:03:20,773
You know, banging on and on
about his dead sister.

743
01:03:22,483 --> 01:03:24,318
No, no. That's all right.

744
01:03:25,528 --> 01:03:28,072
He was talking about Sarah.
What was he saying?

745
01:03:28,239 --> 01:03:31,826
He kept on asking me and asking me
how she died and I didn't know.

746
01:03:34,328 --> 01:03:35,830
An accident.

747
01:03:38,415 --> 01:03:41,544
Yeah, well, he got quite irate
about it all and...er...

748
01:03:41,752 --> 01:03:44,630
...luckily the Old Bill steamed in.

749
01:03:44,839 --> 01:03:48,676
They nicked him. They chased him
up on the bloody roof and nicked him.

750
01:03:48,884 --> 01:03:51,846
They told me...
They told me it was for Dave's own good.

751
01:03:51,971 --> 01:03:53,389
He needed help.

752
01:03:53,556 --> 01:03:56,058
He was a danger to the public
and they was right.

753
01:03:56,225 --> 01:03:57,434
Ta.

754
01:04:00,312 --> 01:04:04,275
Tips up here, right,
a couple of days ago, acting all weird.

755
01:04:04,441 --> 01:04:06,152
Asking about me.

756
01:04:06,318 --> 01:04:08,696
The creepy sod,
he follows me all the way home.

757
01:04:10,239 --> 01:04:13,242
I walk in and there he is,
sitting in my flat.

758
01:04:14,326 --> 01:04:16,328
Like fucking Batman.

759
01:04:17,329 --> 01:04:19,206
He breaks my fucking nose,

760
01:04:19,373 --> 01:04:21,000
talks a load of shit at me

761
01:04:21,167 --> 01:04:22,668
and then buggers off.

762
01:04:22,877 --> 01:04:24,545
What was he saying?

763
01:04:30,009 --> 01:04:31,886
He gave me an address.

764
01:04:32,011 --> 01:04:33,512
An address?

765
01:04:39,643 --> 01:04:42,855
He said that someone was coming
to look him up.

766
01:04:45,608 --> 01:04:48,277
He didn't say anything about it
being his old man.

767
01:04:48,444 --> 01:04:49,445
Please?

768
01:04:50,821 --> 01:04:53,449
Bill, I'll leave the keys on my desk. OK?

769
01:04:53,616 --> 01:04:56,035
That's fine. Thanks, Teri. Good night.

770
01:04:59,330 --> 01:05:00,164
Look...

771
01:05:00,331 --> 01:05:02,958
Dave, he said he'd come back
and finish me off.

772
01:05:03,959 --> 01:05:06,879
So, if it's you or the police
that finds him first,

773
01:05:07,004 --> 01:05:10,549
just make sure that he stays
the fucking hell away from me.

774
01:05:10,716 --> 01:05:12,218
Here.

775
01:05:20,976 --> 01:05:22,853
Who's Franklyn?

776
01:05:23,521 --> 01:05:25,523
That's the address. All right?

777
01:05:26,524 --> 01:05:27,983
My job's done.

778
01:06:01,392 --> 01:06:03,394
Emilia?

779
01:06:04,603 --> 01:06:06,063
Are you all right?

780
01:06:06,230 --> 01:06:09,233
You didn't mention you were coming by.
Come and say hello.

781
01:06:09,400 --> 01:06:12,570
No, thanks. I need to speak to you.
It won't take long.

782
01:06:12,778 --> 01:06:15,197
Darling, I'm in the middle of...

783
01:06:17,950 --> 01:06:20,411
- What is it, sweetheart?
- I'll be in the study.

784
01:06:23,998 --> 01:06:25,791
I'm so sorry. I...

785
01:06:26,459 --> 01:06:28,085
Please excuse me.

786
01:06:34,675 --> 01:06:37,511
What are you doing here?
You knew I had guests.

787
01:06:37,678 --> 01:06:40,097
- Please, Mother, sit down.
- I beg your pardon?

788
01:06:40,264 --> 01:06:42,892
The sooner you sit,
the sooner I'll be gone.

789
01:06:53,778 --> 01:06:55,571
Well?

790
01:06:57,615 --> 01:06:59,909
I want to talk about fairy tales.

791
01:07:27,812 --> 01:07:31,398
If a god is willing to prevent evil,
but not able,

792
01:07:31,565 --> 01:07:33,943
then he is not omnipotent.

793
01:07:34,109 --> 01:07:37,905
If he is able but not willing,
then he must be malevolent.

794
01:07:38,989 --> 01:07:43,410
If he's neither able or willing,
then why call him a god?

795
01:07:48,040 --> 01:07:51,252
Why else do bad things happen
to good people?

796
01:07:54,672 --> 01:07:56,674
I...

797
01:07:57,925 --> 01:08:00,386
I always remembered it
as bedtime stories.

798
01:08:01,387 --> 01:08:03,556
But bad ones.

799
01:08:03,764 --> 01:08:06,767
Stories with horrible endings.

800
01:08:06,934 --> 01:08:09,937
- Emilia...
- Instead of "happy ever after",

801
01:08:10,104 --> 01:08:13,566
the Princess would wake up...

802
01:08:14,608 --> 01:08:16,610
..and her Prince...

803
01:08:17,611 --> 01:08:20,072
..would have left her.

804
01:08:22,575 --> 01:08:24,952
What do you want from me, Emilia?

805
01:08:25,161 --> 01:08:27,121
I want you to admit...

806
01:08:28,831 --> 01:08:30,499
..that you knew about it.

807
01:08:30,666 --> 01:08:32,293
That you remember.

808
01:08:32,460 --> 01:08:36,172
That you've had to live with it all this time,
just like I have.

809
01:08:36,338 --> 01:08:37,965
That's all.

810
01:08:39,842 --> 01:08:44,847
Is this what it's all been about?

811
01:08:45,014 --> 01:08:49,810
The way your father treated you?

812
01:08:49,977 --> 01:08:53,189
I just wanted you to be on my side.

813
01:09:07,161 --> 01:09:09,955
He had a business trip.

814
01:09:10,122 --> 01:09:11,832
Usually, I hated him going away,

815
01:09:11,999 --> 01:09:14,877
but this one was a godsend.

816
01:09:15,044 --> 01:09:19,173
The moment his foot was out of the door,
I packed everything up and took you away.

817
01:09:20,216 --> 01:09:22,218
Just like that.

818
01:09:23,302 --> 01:09:26,639
I hoped we'd...we'd both forget,

819
01:09:27,932 --> 01:09:30,267
move on.

820
01:09:34,814 --> 01:09:36,982
Emilia?

821
01:09:56,460 --> 01:09:58,754
Thank you.

822
01:09:58,921 --> 01:10:02,424
I have to go now.
I have a project to finish.

823
01:10:11,559 --> 01:10:13,769
- Peter.
- Mr Tarrant.

824
01:10:13,936 --> 01:10:15,938
- Please have a seat.
- Thank you.

825
01:10:17,314 --> 01:10:23,195
This is Frank Grant,
David's Military Welfare Officer.

826
01:10:23,320 --> 01:10:25,114
I hope you don't mind if he joins us.

827
01:10:25,281 --> 01:10:27,158
Mr Esser.

828
01:10:28,200 --> 01:10:33,330
Peter, on the whole, we both felt it would
have been wiser if you'd stayed at home.

829
01:10:35,291 --> 01:10:39,712
When you find David...
what will happen?

830
01:10:39,879 --> 01:10:43,549
Well, obviously, he'll be returned
to this institution immediately.

831
01:10:44,758 --> 01:10:48,179
He was getting so much better.
The letter you sent...

832
01:10:48,304 --> 01:10:50,973
David's home visit
is a little redundant now.

833
01:10:52,641 --> 01:10:58,022
As I told you, David took advantage
of his assessment hearing to escape.

834
01:10:59,356 --> 01:11:03,068
He was being fitted with a tag
when he went out of control.

835
01:11:04,487 --> 01:11:05,738
What?

836
01:11:07,323 --> 01:11:09,575
What...what is it? What's happened?

837
01:11:09,784 --> 01:11:14,872
Mr Esser, your son assaulted
two hospital orderlies...

838
01:11:17,458 --> 01:11:20,419
..one of whom
died of his injuries this morning.

839
01:11:21,337 --> 01:11:24,381
We also have reason to believe

840
01:11:24,548 --> 01:11:27,635
there's a chance
he may still have his service weapon.

841
01:11:28,803 --> 01:11:30,763
Essentially, he's possibly armed.

842
01:11:32,973 --> 01:11:35,643
Are you ready to listen to us now, Peter?

843
01:12:34,326 --> 01:12:37,246
Mr Tarrant, if I...

844
01:12:37,413 --> 01:12:39,373
If I talk to David...

845
01:12:41,167 --> 01:12:43,169
..talk some sense into him...

846
01:12:44,503 --> 01:12:46,630
..would you at least reconsider?

847
01:12:49,550 --> 01:12:54,096
Peter, if you have any idea where David is,
you have to tell us.

848
01:12:54,263 --> 01:12:56,265
The police are involved now.

849
01:12:57,057 --> 01:13:00,478
I...I...I don't know where he is.

850
01:13:02,188 --> 01:13:05,357
Your daughter was killed
playing in the street outside your house

851
01:13:05,483 --> 01:13:08,486
just two weeks
before David came back from Iraq.

852
01:13:08,652 --> 01:13:11,822
What's Sarah got to do with it?
Why are you talking about this?

853
01:13:11,989 --> 01:13:14,074
We think it's key to David's condition.

854
01:13:15,785 --> 01:13:20,331
It was clear from his evaluation
that he holds an individual responsible.

855
01:13:20,456 --> 01:13:24,168
Now, you wouldn't happen to know
who that might be?

856
01:13:24,335 --> 01:13:26,128
You?

857
01:13:26,295 --> 01:13:28,631
God, maybe?

858
01:13:29,632 --> 01:13:33,552
It was God's will
that Sarah was taken from us.

859
01:13:33,761 --> 01:13:37,348
We spoke to Anne earlier today, Peter.

860
01:13:37,473 --> 01:13:40,810
She seemed to think
that you were fairly convinced

861
01:13:40,976 --> 01:13:43,187
of God's hand in finding David.

862
01:13:43,354 --> 01:13:46,232
- Your ex-wife thinks you're deluded.
- Frank!

863
01:13:46,398 --> 01:13:49,485
What are you saying?
Why would she say that?

864
01:13:50,861 --> 01:13:53,447
I came here to help.

865
01:13:53,572 --> 01:13:56,158
To help bring my son back home.

866
01:13:56,325 --> 01:14:00,579
Peter, if he does in any way
hold you responsible,

867
01:14:00,788 --> 01:14:02,790
however mistaken...

868
01:14:03,874 --> 01:14:07,044
..there's no telling what he might do,
if you approached him.

869
01:14:08,504 --> 01:14:11,507
We have been severely tested
as a family, Mr Tarrant.

870
01:14:14,385 --> 01:14:16,387
But I have trust in God.

871
01:14:17,805 --> 01:14:21,058
I...I should go back to Cambridge.

872
01:14:21,976 --> 01:14:26,522
I...I think you're right.
I...I should wait for him there.

873
01:14:27,356 --> 01:14:28,524
Thank you.

874
01:14:28,691 --> 01:14:31,152
Thank you very much. Thank you.

875
01:14:32,194 --> 01:14:34,447
Good evening.

876
01:14:34,572 --> 01:14:37,616
So, Wormsnakes told me
he delivered my message.

877
01:14:37,783 --> 01:14:40,744
I decided to give the
little traitor his life.

878
01:14:41,537 --> 01:14:45,749
In a way, I wanted tonight's
assassination to be unique.

879
01:14:45,916 --> 01:14:47,209
Pure.

880
01:14:48,836 --> 01:14:51,964
It felt like the last pieces of
the jigsaw were falling into place.

881
01:14:52,131 --> 01:14:56,302
But don't get me wrong.
This wasn't fate.

882
01:14:58,679 --> 01:15:03,601
For every soul of this deluded population
who believed in fate's comic clockwork,

883
01:15:03,809 --> 01:15:07,563
they neglect to see the wear and tear
beneath the surface.

884
01:15:07,771 --> 01:15:10,483
The teeth that grind into the cogs.

885
01:15:11,400 --> 01:15:14,361
The damage that fate causes so many
in its selfish journey

886
01:15:14,528 --> 01:15:18,157
towards just one favourable consequence.

887
01:15:20,493 --> 01:15:24,121
The Individual had simply run out of luck,
and I was here to collect.

888
01:16:54,336 --> 01:16:57,173
- Hello?
- Hello. Yes. David? Hello?

889
01:16:57,339 --> 01:16:58,799
No. You've got the wrong...

890
01:17:02,678 --> 01:17:06,056
David? Is that you?

891
01:17:07,349 --> 01:17:12,897
Hello? David, please. We've got to talk.
I don't care what you've done.

892
01:17:15,941 --> 01:17:19,153
Listen, I'll be across the road,
in the restaurant.

893
01:17:20,905 --> 01:17:23,574
For fuck's sake.

894
01:17:57,191 --> 01:17:59,568
- Shit.
- Hello?

895
01:18:03,489 --> 01:18:06,200
Yes?

896
01:18:06,367 --> 01:18:10,079
I'm sorry to bother you,
but I've just moved in upstairs.

897
01:18:12,331 --> 01:18:14,333
Coming.

898
01:18:19,964 --> 01:18:22,341
Hello. John Preest.

899
01:18:22,508 --> 01:18:24,301
Upstairs?

900
01:18:24,468 --> 01:18:26,262
My buzzer doesn't seem to be working.

901
01:18:26,428 --> 01:18:28,097
You've moved in upstairs?

902
01:18:29,306 --> 01:18:33,018
I'm sorry to introduce myself like this,
but it's as good a time as any.

903
01:18:33,185 --> 01:18:35,563
Thanks,
but I was just doing something, and...

904
01:18:36,605 --> 01:18:39,066
I...am expecting someone.

905
01:18:39,984 --> 01:18:41,777
I heard your buzzer go.

906
01:18:41,902 --> 01:18:43,571
Yeah, the intercom's wired up wrong.

907
01:18:44,530 --> 01:18:47,324
A guy just rang asking for David.

908
01:18:47,491 --> 01:18:50,161
He said he's across the road,
at the restaurant.

909
01:18:50,327 --> 01:18:52,705
- The restaurant?
- Yeah.

910
01:18:54,540 --> 01:18:57,001
- You're sure?
- Yeah, the restaurant.

911
01:18:58,294 --> 01:19:01,380
Now, excuse me. I have to go.
Good night.

912
01:20:06,570 --> 01:20:08,614
Hello?

913
01:20:08,823 --> 01:20:09,907
Jesus.

914
01:20:10,074 --> 01:20:12,076
It's me again.

915
01:20:13,160 --> 01:20:15,162
You're not gonna believe this.

916
01:20:47,862 --> 01:20:50,364
- What are you doing?
- Please don't make a sound.

917
01:20:50,531 --> 01:20:52,366
It's better if you don't.

918
01:20:54,034 --> 01:20:56,078
- You hurt me.
- Stay quiet.

919
01:21:07,882 --> 01:21:09,675
Don't be afraid.

920
01:21:09,884 --> 01:21:13,053
I have a simple job to do.
It'll be over soon.

921
01:21:28,235 --> 01:21:30,571
- What's your faith?
- What?

922
01:21:30,780 --> 01:21:35,242
- Your religion. What is it?
- I'm not religious.

923
01:21:41,874 --> 01:21:43,876
How long have you been
in Meanwhile City?

924
01:21:46,378 --> 01:21:48,172
What?

925
01:21:57,181 --> 01:21:59,517
Hello.

926
01:21:59,725 --> 01:22:01,727
Well...

927
01:22:02,895 --> 01:22:05,147
Hello back.

928
01:22:16,242 --> 01:22:19,328
- Meanwhile City?
- Yes.

929
01:22:19,495 --> 01:22:22,039
- Where is that?
- Quiet.

930
01:22:26,710 --> 01:22:30,339
- This is London. Where is it you think...
- Will you shut up?

931
01:22:32,508 --> 01:22:34,468
- Just stay back.
- I'm sorry.

932
01:22:34,635 --> 01:22:36,595
- Stay there.
- I'm sorry.

933
01:22:42,226 --> 01:22:44,228
I feel a bit stupid now.

934
01:22:44,395 --> 01:22:47,022
- Why?
- Why do you think?

935
01:22:47,189 --> 01:22:49,316
There's nothing to feel stupid about.

936
01:22:50,359 --> 01:22:52,695
You always knew, really.

937
01:22:52,903 --> 01:22:55,739
How's the wine?

938
01:22:55,906 --> 01:22:58,200
You want to make small talk now?

939
01:22:58,367 --> 01:23:00,911
If I'm going to have
an imaginary conversation,

940
01:23:01,036 --> 01:23:04,415
I'd like to think it might be
a bit more fucking interesting than this.

941
01:23:09,211 --> 01:23:11,922
- Sorry.
- It's OK.

942
01:23:12,047 --> 01:23:14,216
So, my mum was right?

943
01:23:14,383 --> 01:23:15,926
Kind of.

944
01:23:16,051 --> 01:23:18,929
If you believe in something
strongly enough,

945
01:23:19,054 --> 01:23:21,182
who's to say if it's real or not?

946
01:23:21,348 --> 01:23:22,391
Amen.

947
01:23:22,558 --> 01:23:26,520
- I thought you were an atheist.
- Yeah, very funny.

948
01:23:26,687 --> 01:23:31,066
- So, what happens now?
- Time to tie up loose ends, I guess.

949
01:23:31,233 --> 01:23:33,277
Like what?

950
01:23:33,444 --> 01:23:35,488
It was me who told you that story.

951
01:23:35,654 --> 01:23:38,949
The one about the storyteller
and the princess.

952
01:23:39,074 --> 01:23:41,452
That's been bothering you. Right?

953
01:23:41,619 --> 01:23:44,955
Well, if it was you who told me,
then that means it must have...

954
01:23:45,080 --> 01:23:48,000
Come from you? Sure.

955
01:23:48,125 --> 01:23:51,295
Well, if that's true,
then why don't I understand what it means?

956
01:23:51,462 --> 01:23:53,464
You know.

957
01:23:54,924 --> 01:23:58,052
Go on. Try.

958
01:24:08,562 --> 01:24:10,564
The storyteller was...

959
01:24:11,524 --> 01:24:13,526
..so used to his fantasies that...

960
01:24:14,527 --> 01:24:18,072
..no matter how good his reality was,
it was never enough.

961
01:24:18,197 --> 01:24:20,449
Would never be enough.

962
01:24:20,616 --> 01:24:24,954
You see? The first step to recovery
is understanding the problem.

963
01:24:38,134 --> 01:24:38,759
No!

964
01:24:38,926 --> 01:24:40,553
Agh! No!

965
01:24:48,144 --> 01:24:49,603
What's happening here?

966
01:24:51,397 --> 01:24:53,858
- I have to go now.
- Why?

967
01:24:55,234 --> 01:24:59,155
Can't you feel it? It's nearly time.

968
01:25:25,097 --> 01:25:30,269
Life's too much of an adventure as it is
without making anything else up.

969
01:25:31,228 --> 01:25:33,314
I just wanted to let you know that
before I go.

970
01:25:33,481 --> 01:25:36,609
- Please. Please don't.
- Milo...

971
01:25:36,817 --> 01:25:38,360
You're such a romantic.

972
01:25:40,154 --> 01:25:42,156
Use it for somebody else.

973
01:25:47,203 --> 01:25:50,331
Sally, we can...

974
01:25:50,498 --> 01:25:53,459
No, we can't.

975
01:25:53,626 --> 01:25:56,462
Listen. I don't care.

976
01:25:57,505 --> 01:26:00,174
- I don't care.
- It's for the best.

977
01:26:27,159 --> 01:26:30,913
Mr Preest. Mr Preest!

978
01:26:33,749 --> 01:26:37,294
- What are you doing?
- Go, or I'll kill us both.

979
01:26:38,629 --> 01:26:41,507
If you really knew me,
you'd get out of here right now.

980
01:26:41,715 --> 01:26:43,134
See?

981
01:26:57,898 --> 01:26:59,316
David?

982
01:27:31,724 --> 01:27:34,852
Drop the gun.

983
01:27:59,877 --> 01:28:01,796
What was your name?

984
01:28:04,340 --> 01:28:06,342
Emilia.

985
01:28:08,344 --> 01:28:10,137
David.

986
01:28:12,139 --> 01:28:14,141
In this world my name is David.

987
01:28:23,067 --> 01:28:25,069
I think it's time you left.

988
01:29:35,055 --> 01:29:37,057
Will you be all right?

989
01:29:37,224 --> 01:29:39,226
I'll go and find some help.

990
01:30:03,459 --> 01:30:06,879
- Excuse me. Please...
- Sir, are you OK? Have you been hurt?

991
01:30:07,046 --> 01:30:09,215
- No, I'm fine.
- Well, hold on. We'll get to you.

992
01:30:09,381 --> 01:30:11,884
No, you don't understand.
Someone's been shot.

993
01:30:12,051 --> 01:30:15,012
- What? Where?
- Him.

994
01:30:35,241 --> 01:30:37,201
You're hurt.

995
01:34:53,332 --> 01:34:56,627
# This land
# Is ahead of its time

996
01:34:56,794 --> 01:35:01,090
# Oh, but you know it's past its prime
in so many ways

997
01:35:03,425 --> 01:35:06,554
# This land
# Is a miserable rock

998
01:35:06,720 --> 01:35:08,889
# Stuck like a foot at the end of a sock

999
01:35:09,056 --> 01:35:11,058
# Full of razor blades

1000
01:35:13,894 --> 01:35:17,606
# Is mine
# The right to defend at all

1001
01:35:18,524 --> 01:35:22,653
# Is mine
# To fight to the end, I know

1002
01:35:22,820 --> 01:35:28,033
# My hand
# Can hold back the seas no more

1003
01:35:28,200 --> 01:35:30,119
# But it's not from man

1004
01:35:30,286 --> 01:35:33,497
# That we need defending

1005
01:35:33,664 --> 01:35:37,209
# Cos you don't need your weapons now

1006
01:35:37,376 --> 01:35:41,755
# You've got to hold on to your world

1007
01:35:43,424 --> 01:35:46,552
# So, stop and put your weapons down

1008
01:35:47,303 --> 01:35:52,057
# You've got to hold on to your world

1009
01:35:52,224 --> 01:35:54,518
# This fading world

1010
01:36:02,610 --> 01:36:05,404
# This land
# Has damaged the world

1011
01:36:05,571 --> 01:36:09,325
# How many times these bells have tolled
I've heard many tales

1012
01:36:12,411 --> 01:36:15,414
# This land
# Is riddled with lies

1013
01:36:15,581 --> 01:36:20,503
# How many told how the seas
would rise with such heavy scales

1014
01:36:22,546 --> 01:36:27,176
# Is mine
# To know what I've seen and done

1015
01:36:27,343 --> 01:36:31,931
# Is mine
# The suffering and screams at home

1016
01:36:32,097 --> 01:36:36,936
# My hand
# Can't find New Orleans at all

1017
01:36:37,103 --> 01:36:42,358
# This desperate land
that seems to be ending

1018
01:36:42,525 --> 01:36:46,028
# Cos you don't need your weapons now

1019
01:36:46,195 --> 01:36:50,407
# You've got to hold on to your world

1020
01:36:52,618 --> 01:36:56,038
# So, stop and put your weapons down

1021
01:36:56,205 --> 01:37:00,376
# You've got to hold on to your world

1022
01:37:01,210 --> 01:37:03,212
# This fading world

1023
01:37:21,355 --> 01:37:32,575
# This land

1024
01:37:41,375 --> 01:37:47,548
# Is mine

